first do npm init -y to initialize package.json(it manages
dependencies and contains the project name, version, description, author, license, etc.)


after that do 
[npm i express : What it Does:
                Installs the Express package, a web framework for Node.js.

                Adds express to the dependencies field in package.json.

npm i ejs : What it Does:
                Installs the EJS (Embedded JavaScript) templating engine.

                Adds ejs to the dependencies field in package.json.

npm i mongoose : What it Does:
                Installs Mongoose, an Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for MongoDB and Node.js.
                
                Adds mongoose to the dependencies field in package.json.] 

npm i ejs-mate : What it Does:
                Allows you to define a common layout for your application (e.g., a consistent header, footer, or sidebar).
                
                You can use a base file (like layout.ejs) to wrap around your content, avoiding repetitive code in each view.